window.QUESTIONS_2024A=[{"id":1,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the combination of terms or phrases to be inserted into blanks A through C in the description below concerning a method for representing information?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"analogdigitalanalog"},{"key":"B","text":"analogdigitaldigital"},{"key":"C","text":"digitalanaloganalog"},{"key":"D","text":"digitalanalogdigital"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"Analog data varies continuously, while digital data uses discrete numeric values. A music CD records sampled and encoded information digitally, so the blanks are analog, digital, and digital. Continuous physical quantities are analog, discrete numerical representations are digital, and a CD stores music in digital form."},{"id":2,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Japanese restaurants in Sapporo and Japanese restaurants in Hakodate are to be searched for together. Which of the following is the logical expression that represents the search condition?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(“Sapporo” AND “Hakodate”) AND “Japanese restaurant”"},{"key":"B","text":"(“Sapporo” AND “Hakodate”) OR “Japanese restaurant”"},{"key":"C","text":"(“Sapporo” OR “Hakodate”) AND “Japanese restaurant”"},{"key":"D","text":"(“Sapporo” OR “Hakodate”) OR “Japanese restaurant”"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"The search must accept either city name but must also require the phrase “Japanese restaurant.” Therefore, OR joins the city names and AND joins that result with the restaurant term. A result may contain Sapporo or Hakodate, and it must also contain “Japanese restaurant.”"},{"id":3,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"As shown in the figure below, decimal numbers 2, 5, 10, and 21 are represented using five (5) squares that are black or white.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"20"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"30"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-03.png","explanation":"Compare patterns that share black squares. The pattern for 21 contains the pattern for 5 plus the leftmost square, so that square is worth 21 − 5 = 16. Similarly, the second square from the left is worth 10 − 2 = 8. The requested pattern therefore represents 16 + 8 = 24. No assumption about all five positional weights is needed. The leftmost two squares have values 16 and 8, and 16 + 8 = 24."},{"id":4,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When a path goes from node A1 to node C2 in Fig. 1 and the passing nodes are counted as shown in Fig. 2, there are three shortest paths with the minimum number of passing nodes. How many shortest paths are there available to go from node A1 to node D4 via node C2?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"20"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"A shortest route through C2 is formed by independently choosing a shortest path from A1 to C2 and then one from C2 to D4. There are 3 paths to C2. From C2 to D4, the three moves are one vertical and two horizontal, giving 3 arrangements. Thus 3 × 3 = 9. There are 3 shortest paths from A1 to C2 and 3 from C2 to D4, so there are 3 × 3 = 9 routes via C2."},{"id":5,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning machine language?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A program that is written in Fortran or C is converted into machine language and then executed."},{"key":"B","text":"Machine language is a high-level language."},{"key":"C","text":"Machine language expresses a program with sequences of decimal numbers."},{"key":"D","text":"Most of application software is still programmed in machine language."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-04.png","explanation":"A CPU directly executes machine-language instructions. Programs written in high-level languages such as Fortran or C must therefore be translated, usually by a compiler, into machine code before execution. Fortran and C are high-level languages, and their programs are translated into machine language for the processor to execute."},{"id":6,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A power company charges electricity bill shown in the table below.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(units - 100) × 5100 × 5 +(units - 100) × 10 +(units - 200) × 15"},{"key":"B","text":"(units - 100) × 5100 × 5 +200 × 10 +(units - 300) × 15"},{"key":"C","text":"units × 5100 × 5 +(units - 100) × 10 +(units - 200) × 15"},{"key":"D","text":"units × 5100 × 5 +200 × 10 +(units - 300) × 15"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"The rate is progressive by usage band. All bill amounts below are in cents (1/100 US dollars). For at most 100 units, the bill is units × 5. Above 300 units, charge 100 × 5 for the first band, 200 × 10 for the next band, and (units − 300) × 15 for the remainder. A charges every first-band unit at 5, and B separately charges the first 100, next 200, and only the units above 300."},{"id":7,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In a markup language, with the purpose of displaying on a screen and printing, it is possible to directly embed not only the document content, but also the document structure and layout information, and the character font and size information. Which of the following is classified into such a markup language?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"C"},{"key":"B","text":"HTML"},{"key":"C","text":"SQL"},{"key":"D","text":"URL"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-05.png","explanation":"A markup language embeds tags or other markup in content to describe document structure and presentation. HTML is the listed language designed to mark up web documents. HTML uses markup elements to describe the structure and presentation-related meaning of web content."},{"id":8,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The procedure draw receives a non-negative integer number n for input. When the value of n is 6, the procedure outputs the six lines shown below. Which of the following is an appropriate combination of pieces of code to be inserted in A and B in the program?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"i ← 1i ← i + 1"},{"key":"B","text":"k ← 1k ← k + 1"},{"key":"C","text":"i ← i + 1i ← k"},{"key":"D","text":"k ← k + 1k ← i + 1"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-06.png","explanation":"For each output line, the inner-loop counter must restart at 1 and increase by 1 until it reaches the current line number i. Thus A initializes k to 1 and B increments k. Setting k to 1 starts each line at 1, and k ← k + 1 prints the sequence through i and then terminates the inner loop."},{"id":9,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"On a desk that is only large enough to place four (4) files at the same time, six (6) files, A through F, are used to perform a task. When four (4) files are already placed on the desk, the least recently used file must be placed back into the drawer before the fifth file is placed on the desk. When the files are used in the sequence A, B, C, D, B, A, E, A, B, F, which of the following is the last file placed back into the drawer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"B"},{"key":"C","text":"D"},{"key":"D","text":"E"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"Apply least recently used (LRU) replacement by updating recency whenever a file is accessed. After A, B, C, D, B, A, E, A, B, the files on the desk are D, E, A, B and D is the least recently used. Accessing F therefore removes D last. C is removed when E is loaded; after the later A and B accesses, D is the least recently used and is removed for F."},{"id":10,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When USB memory or other such external recordable media is connected to a PC, which of the following is an OS function that automatically executes programs or plays movies on the media and can also cause malware infection?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Autocorrect"},{"key":"B","text":"Autocomplete"},{"key":"C","text":"Auto filter"},{"key":"D","text":"Autorun"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"The exam describes Autorun, a feature that can launch programs or content from inserted media. Actual automatic execution depends on the OS version, media type and policy; it may be blocked or require confirmation. In practice, do not run unfamiliar programs from untrusted media."},{"id":11,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning deep learning?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a method for studying according to proficiency level that uses textbooks published on the Internet and is not restricted by geographical location nor time."},{"key":"B","text":"A computer analyzes a large volume of data, finds patterns, and makes inferences or decisions by itself by using a neural network."},{"key":"C","text":"An appropriate response is provided based on specialist knowledge in specific fields that are systematically categorized."},{"key":"D","text":"The level of difficulty and the knowledge and skills required of each individual to solve problems are estimated according to his/her proficiency level and understanding."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-07.png","explanation":"Deep learning is a machine-learning approach that uses multilayer neural networks to learn patterns from large amounts of data and then make predictions, inferences, or decisions. Learning patterns from large datasets with neural networks and using them for inference or decisions is deep learning."},{"id":12,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning a device driver that enables the use of peripheral devices with a PC?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"When a hard disk drive is initialized and the operating system is reinstalled, it is necessary to reinstall device drivers that were installed separately to the operating system."},{"key":"B","text":"When new application software is installed, it is necessary to reinstall all device drivers that this software uses."},{"key":"C","text":"Even if a device driver is no longer required, a user cannot delete the device driver once it is installed."},{"key":"D","text":"It is only necessary to install one (1) device driver for a printer to use all printers regardless of manufacturer or model."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"A device driver is software that lets the operating system control a particular hardware device. Drivers installed separately from the OS may need to be installed again after the disk is initialized and the OS is reinstalled. In the stated clean installation, initializing the disk removes the separately installed drivers. Required device drivers must therefore be installed again after the OS is restored."},{"id":13,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a description about a technology that improves the processing performance of a computer and is also called turbo boost?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is placed between the CPU and the main memory, and it remedies the slow performance of the main memory in reading and writing."},{"key":"B","text":"It increases the operation frequency of the cores when the heat that the CPU generates and the power that the CPU consumes have certain margins against their limits."},{"key":"C","text":"It provides multiple sections that serve as cores for performing calculations within the CPU, and it executes several processes simultaneously."},{"key":"D","text":"It shares the CPUs of multiple computers, and executes a large amount of processes in a distributed manner."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"Turbo boost temporarily raises a CPU core's operating frequency when temperature, electrical power, and other operating limits have sufficient headroom. Turbo boost raises core frequency when thermal and power margins allow it."},{"id":14,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Two (2) HDDs are connected to a server for storing data. When at least one (1) of the HDDs is working, stored data needs to be available. Which of the following is an appropriate configuration that should be used for the HDDs?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Striping"},{"key":"B","text":"Data mining"},{"key":"C","text":"Tethering"},{"key":"D","text":"Mirroring"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-08.png","explanation":"The requirement says data must remain available if either one of the two disks is still working. Mirroring stores the same data on both disks, so one copy survives a single-disk failure. Mirroring duplicates the data on both HDDs, allowing access from the surviving disk after one fails."},{"id":15,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of parallel processing?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is the division of a series of processing into processing units that can be executed simultaneously, and the execution of these on multiple CPUs."},{"key":"B","text":"It is the execution of multiple related processes that are grouped together as a single process."},{"key":"C","text":"It is the performing of business logic and database processes on the server side, and the performing of user interface processes on the client side."},{"key":"D","text":"It is the division of processing time for a single CPU into short units, and the sequential allocation of these to multiple applications for execution."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"Parallel processing divides work into units that can run at the same time and executes those units on multiple CPUs or cores, reducing elapsed time when the work can be parallelized. Splitting a task into simultaneously executable units and assigning them to multiple CPUs is parallel processing."},{"id":16,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following includes all the appropriate measures to enable the execution of processing even in the event of a failure in part of a system?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(1), (3)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1), (4)"},{"key":"C","text":"(2), (3)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2), (4)"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-09.png","explanation":"The official answer is b: measures (1) and (4). Mirrored disks and a redundant power arrangement help the system continue operating when a component fails. Reducing maintenance in (2) does not provide fault tolerance. Excluding (3) is consistent with reading 'a single high-speed line' as replacing redundant physical paths with one physical line; the question does not establish that interpretation unambiguously. ITPEC Exams note: Combining links into one logical channel is different from replacing them with one physical line. A correctly configured EtherChannel can keep traffic flowing over surviving member links after a link fails. Under that reading, (3) can also support fault tolerance, and none of the offered choices lists all of (1), (3), and (4). This is an explanation of the wording's ambiguity, not an official correction; b remains the scoring answer."},{"id":17,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"It is determined whether an examinee passed or failed by evaluating the score for two (2) subjects X and Y with a spreadsheet software program. The score of each subject is entered in cells A2 and B2 of the worksheet. When passing criteria (1) or (2) is met, “Pass” is displayed in cell C2, and otherwise, “Fail” is displayed. Which of the following is the expression that is entered in cell C2?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"IF(AND((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Pass', 'Fail')"},{"key":"B","text":"IF(AND((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Fail', 'Pass')"},{"key":"C","text":"IF(OR((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Pass', 'Fail')"},{"key":"D","text":"IF(OR((A2+B2) ≥ 120, A2 = 100, B2 = 100), 'Fail', 'Pass')"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-10.png","explanation":"The examinee passes when either criterion is true, so the criteria must be joined by OR. Criterion (2) is also satisfied if either A2 or B2 equals 100. The IF function must return “Pass” when the OR condition is true. OR returns true when the total is at least 120, A2 is 100, or B2 is 100, and IF then displays “Pass.”"},{"id":18,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through C below concerning Open Source Software (OSS), which of the following is the list that contains all and only the appropriate descriptions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"A, C"},{"key":"C","text":"B"},{"key":"D","text":"C"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-10.png","explanation":"Open source software provides source code under a license that permits specified uses such as modification and redistribution. It does not require paid maintenance, and copyright normally remains with its owner. Statement A is appropriate because OSS licenses permit source-code modification and redistribution under their terms."},{"id":19,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When directories d1 and d2 are placed on a web server as shown in the figure, which of the following descriptions specifies the reference of the web page file f2.html on directory d2 from the web page file f1.html on directory d1 (current directory)? Here, the reference method of files is as follows.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"./d2/f2.html"},{"key":"B","text":"./f2.html"},{"key":"C","text":"../d2/f2.html"},{"key":"D","text":"d2/../f2.html"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-11.png","explanation":"From d1, first move one level up to the root with “..”, then enter sibling directory d2 and select f2.html. The relative path is therefore ../d2/f2.html. “..” moves from d1 to the root, then d2/f2.html reaches the target file."},{"id":20,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The tax-inclusive prices of products A and B are calculated by using two (2) tax rates that are set in cells D2 and E2 below. The correct expression that should be entered in cell D4 is $B4*(1.0+D$2), but a wrong expression $B4*(1.0+$D$2) was entered. When the expression that was entered in cell D4 is copied to cells D5, E4, and E5, which of the following is the numeric value that is displayed in cell E5?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"525"},{"key":"B","text":"550"},{"key":"C","text":"630"},{"key":"D","text":"660"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"The erroneous reference $D$2 is absolute in both column and row. Copying the formula to E5 changes $B4 to $B5 but leaves $D$2 unchanged. Therefore E5 calculates 600 × (1 + 0.05) = 630. $B4 becomes $B5, while $D$2 remains fixed, giving 600 × 1.05 = 630."},{"id":21,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a web browser that is Open Source Software (OSS)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Apache"},{"key":"B","text":"Firefox"},{"key":"C","text":"Linux"},{"key":"D","text":"Thunderbird"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"Firefox is an open-source web browser. The other choices are open-source technologies too, but they are not web browsers. Firefox is an open-source application for browsing websites."},{"id":22,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an OS function that executes multiple application programs concurrently on a single PC, such as when a file is downloaded from a website while data is processed with spreadsheet software?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Virtual reality"},{"key":"B","text":"Dual core"},{"key":"C","text":"Dual system"},{"key":"D","text":"Multitasking"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"Multitasking is the operating-system capability that schedules multiple application tasks so they appear to run concurrently on one computer. Multitasking lets the OS run and switch among tasks such as a download and spreadsheet processing concurrently."},{"id":23,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an explanation of the printing method of an inkjet printer?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Printing is performed by directly spraying fine ink particles onto the paper."},{"key":"B","text":"Printing is performed by using printing pins or other such component to hit an ink ribbon against the paper."},{"key":"C","text":"Printing is performed by using the print head to heat ink that melts when it is heated."},{"key":"D","text":"Printing is performed by using laser light to make toner adhere to a photosensitive body."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-12.png","explanation":"An inkjet printer forms an image by ejecting very small droplets of liquid ink through nozzles directly onto the paper. Spraying fine ink droplets onto paper is the defining inkjet printing method."},{"id":24,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the copyright protection technology that is used for a DVD-R and an SD card, and allows digital content to be duplicated to recording media only once?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"AR"},{"key":"B","text":"CPRM"},{"key":"C","text":"HDMI"},{"key":"D","text":"MIDI"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"CPRM is a copy-protection scheme for recordable media such as DVD-R and SD cards and can enforce copy-once handling of protected digital content. CPRM provides content protection for recordable media and supports restrictions such as copying protected content only once."},{"id":25,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the unit that represents the resolution when a photograph or a picture is read by a scanner?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dpi"},{"key":"B","text":"fps"},{"key":"C","text":"pixel"},{"key":"D","text":"ppm"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"Scanner resolution is commonly expressed in dots per inch (dpi), indicating how many sample dots are captured along one inch. dpi measures spatial sampling density per inch and is used for scanner resolution."},{"id":26,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"From a “Product” table and “Sales” table that are managed with a relational database, which of the following contains all and only the products where the total sales for each product in May is at least 20,000 yen?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Product A, Product B, Product C"},{"key":"B","text":"Product A, Product B, Product C, Product D"},{"key":"C","text":"Product B, Product C"},{"key":"D","text":"Product C"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-13.png","explanation":"Use SalesDate to select May sales, sum quantities by product, and multiply by price. Product A: (5 + 4) × 2,000 = 18,000 yen; B: (3 + 3) × 4,000 = 24,000; C: 3 × 7,000 = 21,000; D has no May sale. Only B and C reach 20,000 yen. Product B totals 24,000 yen and Product C totals 21,000 yen; both meet the threshold and no other product does."},{"id":27,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a language used for the operation of a relational database?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"FAQ"},{"key":"B","text":"SQL"},{"key":"C","text":"SSL"},{"key":"D","text":"UML"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"SQL is the standard language used to define, query, insert, update, and otherwise operate on data in relational databases. SQL is used to operate relational databases."},{"id":28,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning foreign keys in a relational database?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A property held by the foreign key is called a unique constraint."},{"key":"B","text":"Duplicate values cannot be set in the fields that are set as foreign keys."},{"key":"C","text":"Multiple foreign keys can be defined in a single table."},{"key":"D","text":"Multiple fields cannot be collectively set as a single foreign key."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"A foreign key links rows to a candidate key, usually a primary key, in another or the same table. A table can contain several foreign keys, duplicates may occur, and a foreign key can consist of multiple columns. One table can define multiple foreign keys, each representing a different relationship."},{"id":29,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When designing a database, which of the following is used for the purpose of organizing and representing the relation of data?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"E-R diagram"},{"key":"B","text":"Arrow diagram"},{"key":"C","text":"Gantt chart"},{"key":"D","text":"Flowchart"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"An entity-relationship (E-R) diagram models data entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities, so it is used in database design. An E-R diagram organizes and represents data structures and relationships for database design."},{"id":30,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate combination of terms or phrases to be inserted into blanks A and B in the description below concerning NAT?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"private IP addressesa MAC address"},{"key":"B","text":"private IP addressesa global IP address"},{"key":"C","text":"host namesa MAC address"},{"key":"D","text":"host namesa global IP address"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-14.png","explanation":"NAT translates addresses between a private network and the public Internet, typically converting private IP addresses used in a LAN to a global IP address and back. NAT maps private IP addresses on the LAN side to a global IP address for Internet communication."},{"id":31,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When another network such as the Internet is accessed from a network in an office or a household, which of the following fulfills the role of an entrance or an exit to the other network?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Splitter"},{"key":"B","text":"Default gateway"},{"key":"C","text":"Hub"},{"key":"D","text":"Repeater"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"A default gateway is the router a host sends traffic to when no more specific route matches the destination. In a typical office or home LAN, it provides the route to external networks such as the Internet. The default gateway forwards traffic between the local network and external networks such as the Internet."},{"id":32,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning encryption of communication when a website with the URL beginning with “https://” is browsed through a PC browser?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Only the communication from the PC to the web server is encrypted."},{"key":"B","text":"Only the communication from the web server to the PC is encrypted."},{"key":"C","text":"The bi-directional communication between the web server and PC is encrypted."},{"key":"D","text":"The direction in which communication will be encrypted depends on the settings of the web server."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"HTTPS uses TLS to protect the session between the browser and web server. Once established, application data traveling in both directions over that connection is encrypted. TLS encrypts the bidirectional communication between the browser and the web server."},{"id":33,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When transmitted over the Internet, data is divided into blocks, each of which is transmitted with a header that specifies the destination, the block number, and an error detecting code. Which of the following is the term for such blocks of data?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Domain"},{"key":"B","text":"Packet"},{"key":"C","text":"Port"},{"key":"D","text":"Router"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"A packet is a block of data sent across a packet-switched network together with control information in headers, such as destination and sequencing information. A packet is a transmitted block containing payload plus header information for delivery and control."},{"id":34,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A DHCP server has been installed in a LAN. When a PC that automatically acquires information from the DHCP server is to be connected to the LAN, which of the following will be set in the PC?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"IP address"},{"key":"B","text":"Latest virus definition file"},{"key":"C","text":"Address list of spam mail"},{"key":"D","text":"Mail addresses assigned by the Internet service provider"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-15.png","explanation":"DHCP automatically supplies network configuration to a client, most notably an IP address and often a subnet mask, default gateway, and DNS server information. A DHCP client can automatically receive an IP address from the DHCP server."},{"id":35,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate example of biometric authentication?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Displaying an image of characters that are difficult for a machine to read on a monitor, and having a person read the characters and enter them"},{"key":"B","text":"Having a person enter a password via a software keyboard that is displayed on a touch panel"},{"key":"C","text":"Reading the trail, pressure, and other characteristics of the action when a touch pen is used for a signature"},{"key":"D","text":"Having a person answer a question that only the person knows the answer to"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"Biometric authentication uses measurable physical or behavioral characteristics. Signature dynamics—such as pen movement, pressure, and timing—are behavioral biometric features. The movement and pressure pattern of a person's signature is a behavioral biometric characteristic."},{"id":36,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When a document file attached to a received e-mail is opened on a PC, the PC begins to behave abnormally. Which of the following is an appropriate suspected attack?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"SQL injection"},{"key":"B","text":"Cross-site scripting"},{"key":"C","text":"Shoulder hacking"},{"key":"D","text":"Macro virus"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"A document can contain executable macros. If a malicious macro runs when the attachment is opened and causes abnormal behavior, a macro virus is the appropriate suspicion. A macro virus is malicious code embedded in a macro-enabled document and can execute when the file is opened."},{"id":37,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the activity in A (Act) phase in the PDCA model adopted in an organization that operates an ISMS?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Deciding to make improvements concerning matters such as flaws that are revealed through the monitoring of operational status and the measurement and evaluation of operational results"},{"key":"B","text":"Monitoring operational status, and measuring and evaluating operational results"},{"key":"C","text":"Creating a security policy, establishing an organizational structure, and creating a procedure for achieving the targets that are defined in the security policy"},{"key":"D","text":"Communicating the security policy to employees, installing security equipment and other security measures, and operating them"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-16.png","explanation":"In PDCA, Plan defines controls, Do implements and operates them, Check monitors and evaluates results, and Act decides and applies corrective improvements based on what Check revealed. Deciding improvements in response to monitored and evaluated results is the Act phase."},{"id":38,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an example of an aim of an attacker who infects someone else’s PC with ransomware?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To obtain personal information on the PC via a network"},{"key":"B","text":"To make files on the PC unusable, and to obtain money in exchange from unlocking them"},{"key":"C","text":"To obtain characters typed with the PC keyboard via a network"},{"key":"D","text":"To operate the PC without the user’s permission by sending instructions for operations via a network"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"Ransomware denies access to data, commonly by encrypting files, and demands a ransom in exchange for purported restoration or a decryption key. Making files unusable and demanding money to unlock them is the characteristic ransomware extortion model."},{"id":39,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A private key and a public key were generated as a key pair and a digital certificate for the public key was issued. Which of the following is an appropriate action that should be taken when the private key is leaked?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Reissuing the digital certificate with the same key pair"},{"key":"B","text":"Requesting to the certification authority for revocation of the digital certificate"},{"key":"C","text":"Creating a new key pair for reissuing a certificate due to the expiration of the validity period"},{"key":"D","text":"Continuing using the same digital certificate, because only the private key was leaked"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"A leaked private key means an attacker may impersonate its owner. The associated certificate must be revoked promptly, and normal remediation also requires generating a new key pair before obtaining a replacement certificate. Requesting revocation tells relying parties that the certificate tied to the compromised private key must no longer be trusted."},{"id":40,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following sets conditions for character type, length, etc. used for passwords that are set for accounts on a computer, etc.?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Single sign-on"},{"key":"B","text":"Password crack"},{"key":"C","text":"Password policy"},{"key":"D","text":"One-time password"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-17.png","explanation":"A password policy defines rules for account passwords; the question asks for the name of this rule set, not which rules are best. Policies can specify length and other conditions. Current NIST guidance favors length and checks against compromised passwords, and rejects compulsory character mixtures and routine periodic changes without evidence of compromise. A password policy sets requirements such as character composition and length."},{"id":41,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among confidentiality, integrity, and availability, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the properties that are lost in the information security incident below?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Confidentiality"},{"key":"B","text":"Confidentiality, integrity"},{"key":"C","text":"Integrity, availability"},{"key":"D","text":"Availability"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"Integrity means information remains accurate and complete; availability means it is accessible when needed. Deleted and unrecoverable files damage integrity, while several hours of unusable service damage availability. The incident does not state that unauthorized persons read the data, so confidentiality loss is not established. File deletion and unrecoverable loss affect integrity, and the work stoppage affects availability."},{"id":42,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A problem has been pointed out that the WEP encryption for wireless LANs can be broken easily. Which of the following is an encryption method that does not have the same weakness and is cryptographically stronger?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ESSID"},{"key":"B","text":"S/MIME"},{"key":"C","text":"SSL"},{"key":"D","text":"WPA2"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"WPA2 is a wireless-LAN security standard designed as a stronger replacement for WEP and uses stronger cryptographic protection. WPA2 provides stronger wireless-LAN encryption than WEP and does not share WEP's well-known key-recovery weakness."},{"id":43,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Company A implements risk analysis for its own information assets. The results show that if a nearby river overflows, the server room on the first floor of the company might be flooded. The company considers the possibility of moving the server room, but decides there is almost no risk of a flood because the last time the river overflowed was 100 years ago, and the management decides that no particular countermeasures are taken. Which of the following is the risk treatment for information security that Company A selects?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Risk transfer"},{"key":"B","text":"Risk avoidance"},{"key":"C","text":"Risk acceptance"},{"key":"D","text":"Risk mitigation"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-18.png","explanation":"Risk acceptance means recognizing a risk and deciding to take no additional treatment because its assessed likelihood or impact is considered tolerable. Management knows the flood risk but decides to take no countermeasure, so it accepts the risk."},{"id":44,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The decision is made to digitize a paper-based contact list that only some people are permitted to view, and to manage it as a contact file. Among the measures A through D below, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the appropriate measures against personal information leakage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"Measures against leakage should restrict reading, protect stored content, and securely destroy the obsolete paper copy. A password, encryption, and shredding address confidentiality; server redundancy primarily addresses availability. A restricts access, B protects the file's contents, and D prevents leakage from the discarded paper original."},{"id":45,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the Web browsing practices (1) through (3) below, which of the following is the list that contains all and only the practices that reduce security risks?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"(1), (2)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1), (3)"},{"key":"C","text":"(2)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2), (3)"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"The official answer is c: practice (2) only. Disabling JavaScript prevents browser scripts from running, reducing that attack surface, although it can break website functions. Administrator privileges in (3) can increase the impact of a successful attack. The official key excludes storing credentials in (1); a possible exam interpretation is concern about another person accessing saved credentials, but the question does not specify a shared or unprotected device. ITPEC Exams note: Browser password storage is not inherently unsafe. A protected password manager on a personal device can support strong, unique passwords and reduce reuse. Saving passwords on public or shared devices can expose accounts to other users. Under the protected-personal-device interpretation, (1) can also reduce risk, so a may be reasonable in practice. The published scoring answer remains c; this conditional guidance is not an official correction."},{"id":46,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In software development, which of the following is the appropriate combination of the descriptions A through C concerning testing and testing processes?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ABC"},{"key":"B","text":"ACB"},{"key":"C","text":"BAC"},{"key":"D","text":"CBA"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-19.png","explanation":"Testing levels have different scopes: unit testing examines internal program logic and paths; integration testing checks interfaces among software components; system testing checks the complete system against nonfunctional requirements such as response or operating time. C is unit testing, B is integration testing, and A is system testing."},{"id":47,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following corresponds to software maintenance?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A response time that was measured in a system test did not satisfy the requirement, so tuning was performed on the software."},{"key":"B","text":"As a result of a software acceptance test, a defect was found, so the orderer requested the developer to fix the software."},{"key":"C","text":"A function was found missing in a unit test of a program, so the function was added to the program."},{"key":"D","text":"A defect was reported on software that is running on a production system, so the software was modified."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"Software maintenance modifies software after delivery, for example to correct defects or adapt it to new needs. In this question, modifying the software already running in production is the clear example of corrective maintenance; the other choices describe testing the initial delivery. Modifying software already running in production in response to a reported defect is corrective maintenance."},{"id":48,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate test for a user to confirm by himself/herself whether the delivered software satisfies the requirements?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Acceptance test"},{"key":"B","text":"Integration test"},{"key":"C","text":"System test"},{"key":"D","text":"Unit test"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"An acceptance test is performed by the customer or user to confirm that delivered software satisfies agreed business and functional requirements before acceptance. Acceptance testing lets the user verify that the delivered system meets the requirements."},{"id":49,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A system migration plan was created for the migration from an existing system to a new system. Which of the following is an appropriate item to be described in the system migration plan?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"System selection policy"},{"key":"B","text":"Schedule for parallel operation of the existing and new systems"},{"key":"C","text":"Evaluation criteria for the quality of the deliverables"},{"key":"D","text":"The work history of project members"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"A migration plan describes how and when the transition will occur, including data conversion, cutover, rollback, user preparation, and any period in which the existing and new systems operate in parallel. The schedule for parallel operation is a key migration activity used to reduce cutover risk."},{"id":50,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of refactoring?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Improving internal architecture without changing the functions that software provides"},{"key":"B","text":"Discovering the specifications of software by analysis of its operations, etc."},{"key":"C","text":"Correcting a defect in software so that it performs according to the specifications"},{"key":"D","text":"Modifying software to add a new function on the basis of user requests, etc."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-20.png","explanation":"Refactoring changes the internal structure of software to improve readability, maintainability, or design without changing its externally observable functions. Refactoring improves internal architecture while preserving the software's behavior and provided functions."},{"id":51,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through D below concerning project management in system development, which of the following lists all and only the failures in scope management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"Scope management defines and controls what work and functions the project includes. Starting without defining the functions and omitting necessary project activities are scope failures; underestimated cost and an unrealistically short schedule belong primarily to cost and schedule management. C fails to define required product scope, and D omits required project work, so both are scope-management failures."},{"id":52,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"For software development work, a plan is created to complete it with 10 people in a period of 15 days. However, it became known that only eight (8) members of staff could be obtained for the first five (5) days. In order to complete the work in 15 days as planned, how many staff members are required from the 6-th day? Here, the productivity of each member of staff is the same.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"11"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"14"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"The planned workload is 10 people × 15 days = 150 person-days. The first five days provide 8 × 5 = 40 person-days, leaving 110 person-days. Over the remaining 10 days, 110 ÷ 10 = 11 people are required. Eleven people × 10 days = 110 person-days, which combined with the first 40 gives the required 150."},{"id":53,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning risk management in a project?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Since a project has a predetermined deadline, all risks must be identified at the start of the project."},{"key":"B","text":"Since the realization of a risk has a negative impact to a project, risk measures are planned to avoid all risks."},{"key":"C","text":"In order to plan risk measures, risks are prioritized on the basis of the likelihood of occurrence of an event and its consequences."},{"key":"D","text":"In order to cut down the cost involved in taking action against a risk, risk measures are planned whenever a risk is realized."}],"correct":"C","page":"page-21.png","explanation":"Project risks are prioritized by combining how likely each event is with the size of its consequences. This supports selecting proportionate responses for the most significant risks. Likelihood and consequence are fundamental criteria for assessing and prioritizing risks before planning responses."},{"id":54,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A company orders information system development to an overseas software developer under a contract for software development. Which of the following is an appropriate activity to be performed by the company in project procurement management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"When a defect is found after the acceptance of delivery, even if not indicated in the contract, the company asks the developer to examine not only the defect but similar defects and fix them."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to make good use of the capabilities of the developer, the company does not include the provisions of intellectual property rights in the contract."},{"key":"C","text":"After the start of development, the company has the procurement detail such as the development scope, specifications, and work contents, etc. agreed upon by the developer in writing."},{"key":"D","text":"At the time of signing the contract, the company agrees upon in writing with the developer the documents to be delivered and the rules for changing specifications during development."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"Procurement management requires important deliverables, scope, responsibilities, intellectual-property terms, acceptance, and change-control rules to be agreed in the contract before work proceeds. Agreeing deliverables and specification-change rules in writing at contract signing establishes clear procurement obligations and change control."},{"id":55,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a method to break down the required activities into a hierarchical structure in software development?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"CMM"},{"key":"B","text":"ITIL"},{"key":"C","text":"PERT"},{"key":"D","text":"WBS"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"A work breakdown structure (WBS) decomposes the total project scope and required work into progressively smaller, manageable components arranged hierarchically. WBS is the method for breaking required project activities into a hierarchical structure."},{"id":56,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Quality management in system development projects has a quality planning process to define quality requirements and quality standards for deliverables and to specify the methods for achieving them. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the quality planning process?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"If deliverables are not exactly the same as those of past system development projects, past quality standards cannot be used as reference."},{"key":"B","text":"Since schedules have the highest priority in all projects, it is acceptable to shorten the period for reviewing and testing for achieving target quality."},{"key":"C","text":"Quality should have the highest priory in all projects, and, to enhance the quality of deliverables, constraints should not be placed on the budget."},{"key":"D","text":"The effects such as reductions in reworking, improvement in productivity, improvement of stakeholder satisfaction brought about by achieving targeted quality, and the required costs are to be compared."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-22.png","explanation":"Quality planning balances the cost of achieving target quality against benefits such as less rework, higher productivity, and greater stakeholder satisfaction. Quality, schedule, and budget constraints must be considered together. Comparing the benefits of meeting quality targets with the required prevention, appraisal, and other costs supports rational quality planning."},{"id":57,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In a project, a contingency reserve is the cost that is included in the initial project scope and is prepared for events that are predictable but uncertain. Among the costs that are allocated by the project manager of a company that receives an order for a system development, which of the following is an appropriate cost that can be classified as a contingency reserve?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The cost that is necessary for the replacement of a device when the device happens to fail under the development environment"},{"key":"B","text":"The cost that is necessary for the activities of the project leader who manages the development progress"},{"key":"C","text":"The cost that is necessary for fulfilling the new requirements of users that are outside the scope of the project"},{"key":"D","text":"The cost that is necessary for purchasing the quality management tools of a system that are planned to be adopted in the project"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"A contingency reserve covers identified risks—events that can be foreseen but whose occurrence or exact cost is uncertain. A possible development-device failure is such a known risk. Device failure is a foreseeable but uncertain event, so a planned replacement allowance can be a contingency reserve."},{"id":58,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In a service desk that acts as the point of contact for users, a tool that uses automated response technology is used in addition to telephone and e-mail. Which of the following is the most appropriate example of such a tool?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"FAQ"},{"key":"B","text":"RPA"},{"key":"C","text":"Escalation"},{"key":"D","text":"Chatbot"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"A chatbot converses with users and automatically generates responses, making it suitable as an additional automated service-desk contact channel. A chatbot uses automated response technology to interact with users through text or voice."},{"id":59,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate requirement for the availability of an e-mail service in IT service management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Allowing the e-mail service to be used with only a web browser"},{"key":"B","text":"Allowing the e-mail service to be used anytime except for defined maintenance hours"},{"key":"C","text":"Preventing e-mails addressed to a user from being read by another user without permission"},{"key":"D","text":"Preventing sent e-mails from being falsified"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-23.png","explanation":"Availability concerns whether a service can be accessed and used when required. Being usable at all times except agreed maintenance windows is therefore an availability requirement. Defined service hours excluding planned maintenance directly specify when the email service must be available."},{"id":60,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate purpose of providing FAQ to users in IT service management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Providing a framework of IT service management"},{"key":"B","text":"Defining a target value for the service level on the sides of both service provider and users"},{"key":"C","text":"Establishing a single point of contact for users to make all kinds of queries concerning the service"},{"key":"D","text":"Supporting users so that they can solve problems by themselves"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"FAQs give users ready answers to common questions and troubleshooting steps, enabling self-service without contacting support for every issue. FAQs support users in resolving common questions and problems by themselves."},{"id":61,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the descriptions A through D below, which of the following lists all and only the activities of facility management?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, C"},{"key":"B","text":"A, D"},{"key":"C","text":"B, D"},{"key":"D","text":"C, D"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"Facility management covers the physical environment that supports information systems, including building access and power continuity. Anti-malware and software-license administration are logical or software asset controls rather than facility controls. Controlling access to the computer building and installing a UPS both manage physical facilities and infrastructure."},{"id":62,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate example of criteria for evaluating the service level of a service desk that receives queries from system users over the telephone?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Cost of the service"},{"key":"B","text":"Number of system failures"},{"key":"C","text":"Availability of the system"},{"key":"D","text":"Response time for queries"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"A service-desk service level should measure the performance of the desk's own user-support activity. Time taken to respond to a telephone query is a direct, measurable service-desk indicator. Query response time directly measures how promptly the service desk serves callers."},{"id":63,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of monitoring in internal control?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a process of continuously evaluating if internal control is working effectively."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a process of promoting compliance to the laws and other regulations concerning internal control."},{"key":"C","text":"It is a process of establishing an organization for internal control."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a process of analyzing the risks that hinder internal control."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-24.png","explanation":"Monitoring is the ongoing or periodic evaluation of whether internal controls are present, operating as designed, and continuing to work effectively. Continuously evaluating the effectiveness of internal control is monitoring."},{"id":64,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate measure to enable internal controls?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Preventing creation of a job description indicating the scope of work and roles"},{"key":"B","text":"Preventing creation of a work handover document for a successor"},{"key":"C","text":"Preventing processing of purchasing and payment by the same person"},{"key":"D","text":"Preventing separation of team members for system development and system operation"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"Segregation of duties reduces fraud and error by preventing one person from controlling incompatible steps of a transaction. Separating purchasing from payment is a standard internal-control measure. Separating purchasing and payment prevents one person from both initiating and completing the same financial transaction."},{"id":65,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate description of the roles of a system auditor?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Preparing a workflow, work description, and risk control matrix that reflect the flow and business operations, evaluating the risks, and installing an appropriate system"},{"key":"B","text":"Installing a mechanism for appropriate monitoring and self-inspection in each process of planning, development, operation, and maintenance of the information system, and taking actions to operate the information system smoothly"},{"key":"C","text":"Verifying whether or not the risks of the information system are controlled appropriately and effectively from a standpoint that is independent of the department being audited, and reporting the result to the client"},{"key":"D","text":"Specifying the policies and objectives, and establishing a management system so that the risks of the information system are controlled appropriately"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"A system auditor must be independent of the audited department, objectively assess whether information-system risks and controls are appropriate and effective, and report findings to the audit client. Independent verification of control effectiveness and reporting the result is the core system-auditor role."},{"id":66,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Company A is a large company with multiple offices nationwide, and it created BCP that envisaged the total destruction of the head office building in a large natural disaster. In consideration of the purpose of the BCP, which of the following is Company A’s most appropriate BCP?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In order to prevent damage by a fire that occurs after a disaster, replacing curtains and other such things with flame-resistant products and planning regular checks of fire prevention equipment"},{"key":"B","text":"In order to swiftly respond to instructions from the head office when a disaster occurs, establishing a procedure to completely halting work at all offices and have all employees standby until an instruction is received from the head office"},{"key":"C","text":"In order to continue business after a natural disaster, specifying an office to take over the functions of the head office, narrowing down the important work that needs to be dealt with, and establishing an implementation procedure for this work"},{"key":"D","text":"Incorporating insurance premiums for the head office building into the annual budget, and preparing for a relocation to a building with the same scale as the current head office"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-25.png","explanation":"A business continuity plan prepares the organization to continue its most important activities after disruption. With the head office destroyed, another office must assume essential functions under a predefined procedure. Naming an alternate office, prioritizing critical work, and defining procedures enables continued business after the disaster."},{"id":67,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an explanation of a balance sheet?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It displays the status of cash flow in a fixed period of time by activity category."},{"key":"B","text":"It displays the management performance of a company by the income and cost generated in a fixed period of time."},{"key":"C","text":"It displays the previous term-end balance, changes during the year, and the current term-end balance for each item of net assets of a company."},{"key":"D","text":"It displays the financial condition of a company on the date of settlement on the basis of the categories of assets, liabilities, and net assets."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"A balance sheet is a snapshot at a particular date showing what a company owns, owes, and the residual owners' interest: assets, liabilities, and net assets. A balance sheet reports assets, liabilities, and net assets at the settlement date."},{"id":68,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"The operating profit when the sales quantity of a product is 700 units is as shown in the table below. When the unit sales price is reduced by 20% to expand sales, the sales quantity increases by 20%. How much, in yen, is the operating profit at this time? Here, the variable cost per one (1) unit of the product does not change.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"200,000"},{"key":"B","text":"204,000"},{"key":"C","text":"260,000"},{"key":"D","text":"320,000"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"Original unit price is 700,000 ÷ 700 = 1,000 yen, and variable cost is 140,000 ÷ 700 = 200 yen per unit. New price is 1,000 × 0.8 = 800 yen and quantity is 700 × 1.2 = 840. Profit is 800 × 840 − 200 × 840 − 300,000 = 204,000 yen. New sales are 672,000 yen, variable cost is 168,000 yen, and fixed cost is 300,000 yen, so profit is 204,000 yen."},{"id":69,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among the phases of the PDCA cycle in corporate business operations, which of the following measures and evaluates the status of operations on the basis of KPI?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"P"},{"key":"B","text":"D"},{"key":"C","text":"C"},{"key":"D","text":"A"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-26.png","explanation":"In PDCA, Check measures actual operation and evaluates performance against plans and targets. KPIs provide the measurements used in this phase. Check measures and evaluates operating status using KPIs."},{"id":70,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Data of the defects and faults of products, complaints from customers, etc. are categorized according to their cause and situation. Which of the following represents the number of data in each category in descending order on a bar graph and the cumulative total on a line graph?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Control chart"},{"key":"B","text":"Tree diagram"},{"key":"C","text":"Pareto chart"},{"key":"D","text":"Matrix chart"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-27.png","explanation":"A Pareto chart orders category frequencies from largest to smallest as bars and overlays a cumulative-percentage or cumulative-total line, helping identify the few causes responsible for most effects. Descending category bars plus a cumulative line define a Pareto chart."},{"id":71,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When the purchase and sales of a product in April are as in the table below, what is the inventory value in yen for the product at the end of April according to the moving average method? The moving average method calculates the average unit price of products in the inventory each time a purchase is made, and uses the average unit price for products in the inventory immediately beforehand for the calculation of the inventory value.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"1,280"},{"key":"B","text":"1,300"},{"key":"C","text":"1,400"},{"key":"D","text":"1,500"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-27.png","explanation":"After April 8, 200 units cost 2,400 yen, so the moving average is 12 yen. The April 18 sale leaves 50 units valued at 50 × 12 = 600 yen. The April 29 purchase adds 50 units costing 800 yen, so ending inventory is 600 + 800 = 1,400 yen for 100 units. The remaining 50 units at 12 yen plus 50 purchased at 16 yen total 600 + 800 = 1,400 yen."},{"id":72,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A person wishes to start at point X, pass through all of points A, B, and C, and arrive at point Y. When the routes and the required times between points are as shown in the figure and the table, what is the shortest time in minutes from point X to point Y? Here, the points A, B, and C may be passed through in any order.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"110"},{"key":"B","text":"130"},{"key":"C","text":"140"},{"key":"D","text":"150"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"The feasible orders visiting each of A, B and C once are X–A–B–C–Y (140 minutes), X–A–C–B–Y (130), X–B–A–C–Y (150) and X–C–A–B–Y (170). Orders ending at A cannot reach Y directly. The minimum is therefore 130 minutes. All travel times are positive, and detours between these intermediate points are no shorter than their direct links, so repeating visits cannot improve the result. X–A–C–B–Y uses the listed links and takes 20 + 30 + 20 + 60 = 130 minutes."},{"id":73,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description of NDA?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is a specialized organization that monitors and analyzes threats to the information systems in a company, etc."},{"key":"B","text":"It is a contract that makes the contracting parties agree to hold and maintain in confidence the confidential information of the other party."},{"key":"C","text":"It is an agreement of an objective quality standard that is concluded between a service provider and the user concerning the service provided."},{"key":"D","text":"It is a hierarchical decomposition of the tasks to be implemented in a project."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-28.png","explanation":"An NDA, or non-disclosure agreement, is a contract requiring parties to protect designated confidential information and restrict its disclosure or use. An NDA contractually obligates parties to keep the other party's confidential information secret."},{"id":74,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a code that stores information in a vertical and horizontal two-dimensional pattern?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ASCII code"},{"key":"B","text":"G-code"},{"key":"C","text":"EAN code"},{"key":"D","text":"QR code"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"A QR code is a two-dimensional code whose dark and light modules store information in both horizontal and vertical directions. A QR code stores data in a two-dimensional matrix pattern."},{"id":75,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Concerning the EU’s General Data Protection Rules (GDPR), which of the following lists all and only the appropriate descriptions?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, C"},{"key":"D","text":"A, C, D"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-29.png","explanation":"GDPR, the General Data Protection Regulation, governs personal-data processing. It can apply through an EU establishment, offering goods or services to people in the EU, or monitoring their behavior there. A and C are the intended combination. C assumes no other EU territorial link; an overseas office alone does not guarantee exemption. A and C match the territorial distinction tested, assuming C involves no additional EU link such as monitoring people there."},{"id":76,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Among company’s actions A through C below, which of the following lists all and only the acts that may be problematic in terms of compliance?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A, B"},{"key":"B","text":"A, B, C"},{"key":"C","text":"A, C"},{"key":"D","text":"B, C"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"The published answer is explained by the apparent Japanese consumer-protection context; the question does not explicitly name a jurisdiction. With no purchase or other transaction required, A is an open prize campaign, so the stated prize does not make it the problematic act under that interpretation. B hides paid advertising as editorial content, and C may mislead buyers into thinking a domestic bag was made in France. Thus B and C raise concerns. B is undisclosed advertising, and C can mislead buyers about origin, so both raise compliance concerns."},{"id":77,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is appropriate as an expected advantage of the adoption of ISO 9001 by companies?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The companies’ trade procedures will be standardized, leading to increased efficiency and the avoidance of non-tariff barriers."},{"key":"B","text":"Technical specifications will be standardized in the industry, and increase in product quality and expansion of markets will move forward."},{"key":"C","text":"Methods for handling information assets will be standardized and the quality of information security will increase."},{"key":"D","text":"Business operations concerning quality management will be standardized, and the quality and efficiency of management will increase."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"ISO 9001 specifies requirements for a quality management system. Adoption helps standardize and continually improve quality-related business processes, supporting consistent quality and management efficiency. ISO 9001 supports standardized quality-management operations and improved effectiveness and efficiency."},{"id":78,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an organization in the USA that promotes standardization activities concerning Ethernet LAN and wireless LAN, etc.?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ICANN"},{"key":"B","text":"IEEE"},{"key":"C","text":"ISO"},{"key":"D","text":"W3C"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-30.png","explanation":"IEEE is a US-based professional organization that develops widely used technical standards, including the IEEE 802 family for Ethernet and wireless LANs. IEEE develops IEEE 802.3 Ethernet and IEEE 802.11 wireless-LAN standards."},{"id":79,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate marketing strategy for narrowing down the customer base to focus on by classifying customers on the basis of age, gender, family structure, and the like, and analyzing the purchasing behaviors of each group?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Service marketing"},{"key":"B","text":"Segment marketing"},{"key":"C","text":"Social marketing"},{"key":"D","text":"Mass marketing"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"Segment marketing divides a broad market into groups with shared characteristics or behavior and targets selected groups with an appropriate offer. Classifying customers by demographics and analyzing each group's buying behavior is market segmentation and segment marketing."},{"id":80,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"There are two (2) indicators for evaluating the achievement of strategic goals. These are leading indicators that evaluate the means for achieving the goals, and result indicators that evaluate the degree of goal achievement. If a strategic goal is “acquire new customers,” which of the following is an appropriate leading indicator?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sales increase amount"},{"key":"B","text":"New contract acquisition ratio"},{"key":"C","text":"Total customer increase ratio"},{"key":"D","text":"Number of visits to prospective customers"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"A leading indicator measures actions expected to produce a future result. Visits to prospective customers are an acquisition activity, while sales and customer or contract increases are outcomes. The number of visits to prospective customers measures an activity intended to lead to future customer acquisition."},{"id":81,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of user experience (UX)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The design of a software product with consideration that it is easy to use for as many people as possible, including mainly elderly people and disabled people"},{"key":"B","text":"A method of identifying customers on the basis of analysis of customer data, and deepening relationships with customers by using channels such as call centers and the Internet"},{"key":"C","text":"A software product’s capability that enables efficient use by a user under specified conditions"},{"key":"D","text":"People’s feelings and responses that are gained through the use of a product, system, or service"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"User experience (UX) is the overall perception, emotions, and responses a person has before, during, and after interacting with a product, system, or service. UX encompasses people's feelings and responses arising from using a product, system, or service."},{"id":82,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a system that centrally manages the process from materials procurement to product sales, and aims for the optimization of supply?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ASP"},{"key":"B","text":"CRM"},{"key":"C","text":"ERP"},{"key":"D","text":"SCM"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-31.png","explanation":"Supply chain management (SCM) coordinates the flow of materials, products, information, and related processes from procurement through production and sales to optimize the overall supply chain. SCM manages and optimizes the supply process from materials procurement through product sales."},{"id":83,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Company A performs analysis of its positioning with competitors. In order for Company A to obtain the best evaluation of all three (3) companies, what is the minimum number of points required in the brand evaluation item?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"9"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"Compute weighted totals. Company B scores 1×9 + 4×7 + 3×10 + 2×6 = 79. Company C scores 1×6 + 4×9 + 3×7 + 2×10 = 83. Company A scores 1×10 + 4×10 + 3×6 + 2×Brand = 68 + 2×Brand. To rank above 83, Brand must exceed 7.5, so the minimum integer score is 8. With brand 8, Company A scores 84, exceeding both Company B's 79 and Company C's 83."},{"id":84,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate as the underlying concept of CRM?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The source of profit is an early entry into a market with little competition."},{"key":"B","text":"The source of profit is a good relationship with the customer."},{"key":"C","text":"The source of profit is a shorter product life cycle."},{"key":"D","text":"The source of profit is a large share in a specific market."}],"correct":"B","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"Customer relationship management (CRM) treats strong, continuing customer relationships as a source of long-term value and profit through retention, satisfaction, and appropriate interactions. CRM is founded on creating and maintaining good relationships with customers as a source of business value."},{"id":85,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a technique that increases the potential for success in the development of a new business model or product, by creating the minimum service or product on the basis of a hypothesis, and performing repeated verification of customer value in a short interval of times?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Cannibalization"},{"key":"B","text":"Business operations modeling"},{"key":"C","text":"Digital transformation"},{"key":"D","text":"Lean startup"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-32.png","explanation":"Lean startup tests business assumptions by building a minimum viable product (MVP), measuring customer response, learning, and iterating quickly before committing large resources. Lean startup uses an MVP and rapid build-measure-learn cycles to verify customer value and reduce uncertainty."},{"id":86,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"In call handling at a call center, which of the following is the most appropriate example of the use of AI to implement a more effective FAQ system?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"As part of the training for operators, examples of questions and answers that use the existing FAQ are taught on a web screen."},{"key":"B","text":"According to the numbers that are entered according to the guidance, a call is assigned to an operator with responsibility for the relevant FAQ item."},{"key":"C","text":"From the caller’s telephone number of a received call, customer information and a record of the content and response of past inquiries are retrieved from a customer information database and displayed on the operator’s screen."},{"key":"D","text":"In call handling, emotion and intent are determined from the audio of a question in order to increase the certainty of selection of the optimum candidate response from the FAQ."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"AI can analyze speech content and vocal cues to estimate a caller's intent and emotion, then suggest relevant FAQ answers. These are uncertain inferences, not guaranteed readings of a person's feelings, so the suggestions need appropriate checking. Using speech analysis to estimate intent and emotion and rank FAQ responses is an AI application. Its accuracy depends on the model and the call context."},{"id":87,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is a business objective that becomes possible to achieve with “the introduction of a POS system”?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Improvement in the work productivity of salespersons and organizational strength of the sales department"},{"key":"B","text":"Reduction in inventory volume of component parts and partly finished goods"},{"key":"C","text":"Optimization of the series of processes from procurement to manufacturing, shipment, and sales"},{"key":"D","text":"Improvement in the selection of goods at each store and streamlining of ordering and inventory control"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"A point-of-sale (POS) system captures item-level sales data at checkout. Each store can analyze what sells, improve its assortment, and use current sales information to streamline ordering and inventory control. POS sales data supports store-specific assortment decisions, replenishment, and inventory management."},{"id":88,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of CAD, as used in the manufacturing industry?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It calculates the required quantity of materials for a product manufacturing plan and orders materials."},{"key":"B","text":"It manages information about the components, semi-finished products, quantities, etc. required for the manufacture of products."},{"key":"C","text":"It performs unified management of information such as product blueprints and component tables, from design to manufacturing."},{"key":"D","text":"It uses computers in product design to improve the productivity and reliability of design specifications."}],"correct":"D","page":"page-33.png","explanation":"Computer-aided design (CAD) uses computers to create, modify, analyze, and document product designs, improving design productivity and accuracy or reliability. Using computers directly for product design is CAD."},{"id":89,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is an appropriate case example that corresponds to traceability?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Taking advantage of the Internet and web technology for the use of computers in education"},{"key":"B","text":"Outsourcing all software development to an external specialized company without placing any development department within one’s own company"},{"key":"C","text":"Sharing knowledge and information among employees across the entire organization, and utilizing it effectively to improve business performance"},{"key":"D","text":"Being able to check the history from production up to sales on the basis of the labels pasted on meat and fish products"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"Traceability is the ability to follow an item's history, application, or location through recorded identifiers and process data. Labels that allow checking a food product's history from production through sales provide traceability."},{"id":90,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is classified as a “B to E” transaction?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A company provides services, such as welfare and education for the company’s own employees, through the Internet."},{"key":"B","text":"A travel company uses the Internet to give campaign information and sell tickets to consumers in advance."},{"key":"C","text":"An automobile manufacturer uses the Internet to procure components and materials from vendors across the world."},{"key":"D","text":"In an auction held on the Internet, a participant buys a product from another participant."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"B to E means business-to-employee: electronic services supplied by a company to its own employees. Company-provided welfare and education services for employees are B-to-E transactions."},{"id":91,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A single unit of Product A is composed of three (3) pieces of Part B and two (2) pieces of Part C. In the production plan for a particular period, when the demand for Product A is 10, which of the following is the net requirement of Part B? Here, the quantity in stock is five (5) for Part B, and there are no other pieces in stock, in process, on back order, or already allocated. The net requirement is calculated by subtracting the stock available for allocation from the gross requirement.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"25"},{"key":"C","text":"30"},{"key":"D","text":"45"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-34.png","explanation":"Gross requirement for Part B is 10 products × 3 parts each = 30 parts. Subtract the 5 available parts in stock: 30 − 5 = 25 parts net requirement. Part B requires 30 pieces in total, and 5 available pieces reduce the net requirement to 25."},{"id":92,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"When the spreadsheet shown below is converted into CSV format, which of the following is an appropriate list of data that is generated by spreadsheet software? Here, records are separated by the carriage return code “CR”. The expression in a cell is automatically recalculated, and the resulting value is written back into that cell. Although the entered expressions are shown in row 3 and column C below, the resulting values are actually displayed on the screen.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"2 , 6 , 8 CR 7 , 4 , 11 CR 6 , 13 , 24 CR"},{"key":"B","text":"2 , 6 , 8 CR 7 , 4 , 11 CR 9 , 10 , 19 CR"},{"key":"C","text":"2 , 7 , 6 CR 6 , 4 , 13 CR 8 , 11 , 24 CR"},{"key":"D","text":"2 , 7 , 9 CR 6 , 4 , 10 CR 8 , 11 , 19 CR"}],"correct":"C","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"CSV records correspond to spreadsheet rows and fields to columns, while formulas are replaced by calculated values. C1 = 2 + 4 = 6; C2 = 6 + 7 = 13; A3 = 2 + 6 = 8; B3 = 7 + 4 = 11; C3 = 13 + 11 = 24. The rows are therefore “2,7,6”, “6,4,13”, and “8,11,24”. It preserves rows and columns and writes each formula's calculated result: 2,7,6 CR 6,4,13 CR 8,11,24 CR."},{"id":93,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate utilization of RPA for a company?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The adoption of an important strategy by management, such as an M&A"},{"key":"B","text":"The provision of a service that matches personal tastes"},{"key":"C","text":"The identification of patterns in large volumes of behavioral data concerning potential customers"},{"key":"D","text":"The streamlining of routine administrative work"}],"correct":"D","page":"page-35.png","explanation":"Robotic process automation (RPA) uses software robots to repeat structured, rule-based computer operations, making it well suited to routine administrative work. RPA can automate repetitive data entry, transfer, checking, and other routine office tasks."},{"id":94,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the analysis of big data?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In order to forecast unknown circumstances, analysis that uses machine learning in addition to statistical analysis is also effective."},{"key":"B","text":"Non-textual data in the form of video, images, and audio data cannot be in the scope of analysis."},{"key":"C","text":"Only information that spreads by humans, such as comments on an electronic bulletin board, social media messages, and website search history, is used in the analysis of human actions."},{"key":"D","text":"Data that is not intended to be analyzed, such as a blog entry, is out of the scope regardless of the purpose of analysis."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"Big-data analysis can combine statistical techniques with machine learning to discover complex patterns and make predictions about previously unknown or future situations. Machine learning is effective alongside statistics for prediction and pattern discovery in large, varied datasets."},{"id":95,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following analysis techniques used in Enterprise Architecture (EA) clarifies the issues by comparing the ideal situation with the current situation?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Gap analysis"},{"key":"B","text":"Core competence analysis"},{"key":"C","text":"Value chain analysis"},{"key":"D","text":"Pareto analysis"}],"correct":"A","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"Gap analysis compares a desired or target architecture with the current architecture to identify differences that must be addressed. Gap analysis explicitly identifies the gaps between the current state and the ideal future state."},{"id":96,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is “cloud computing”?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"One of the Internet communication protocols"},{"key":"B","text":"One of the service models for providing computer resources"},{"key":"C","text":"One of the software development methods for flexibly supporting changes in the specification"},{"key":"D","text":"One of the electronic data exchange standards for electronic commercial transactions"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-36.png","explanation":"Cloud computing is a service model that provides shared computing resources—such as servers, storage, platforms, or applications—over a network on demand. It is a model for delivering computing resources as services."},{"id":97,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following is the most appropriate description of the Fourth Industrial Revolution?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The Internet and AI are utilized in a wide range of fields in daily life, such as medical care, infrastructure, and traffic systems, and service automation and quality improvement are achieved."},{"key":"B","text":"Production automation and labor cost reduction are achieved by the introduction to factories of industrial robots that utilize electronics."},{"key":"C","text":"Mass production of industrial products is performed by the construction of production lines that use conveyor belts in factories."},{"key":"D","text":"Productivity is increased compared to manual work by the use of steam energy as the driving force for machinery in light industry, such as sewing machines."}],"correct":"A","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"The Fourth Industrial Revolution is characterized by broad integration of digital networks, AI, IoT, and data into physical and social systems, enabling automation and smarter services. Wide use of the Internet and AI across medicine, infrastructure, transport, and daily life reflects the Fourth Industrial Revolution."},{"id":98,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"At power companies, the amount of electricity consumed by each household is measured remotely by communicating with electrical meters that are connected to the Internet, instead of measured by meter readings by a person. Which of the following is a term that represents the mechanism where a range of devices are connected to the Internet and utilize information in cases such as this?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"EDI"},{"key":"B","text":"IoT"},{"key":"C","text":"ISP"},{"key":"D","text":"RFID"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"The Internet of Things (IoT) connects physical devices and sensors to networks so they can collect, exchange, and use data, as with remotely read smart electricity meters. Internet-connected meters that automatically transmit consumption data are an IoT application."},{"id":99,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"Which of the following are international development targets that are composed of 17 objectives set by the United Nations in order to achieve a sustainable world?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"COP28"},{"key":"B","text":"SDGs"},{"key":"C","text":"UNESCO"},{"key":"D","text":"WHO"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"The Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) are the United Nations' set of 17 global goals for achieving a more sustainable world. SDGs are the 17 international goals for sustainable development."},{"id":100,"session":"2024A","year":2024,"question":"A company planning the development of a business information system decided to present an RFP to SIers. Which of the following must be described in the RFP at a minimum?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The development schedule"},{"key":"B","text":"The functions that should be implemented in the business information system"},{"key":"C","text":"The method for achieving the business information system"},{"key":"D","text":"The project team"}],"correct":"B","page":"page-37.png","explanation":"An RFP (request for proposal) tells potential suppliers what the requester needs. Here it is sent to system integrators, or SIers, which combine components into a working system. Required system functions are essential so suppliers can propose suitable methods, schedules, and teams. The functions to be implemented define the minimum business and system requirements that an RFP must communicate."}];